id: pm-vcs-v5bg
title: Stop concurrent test packs from rewriting the shared build
description: "installPackedExtension ran npm pack --silent in the package root. npm pack runs prepack (npm run build = tsc), which truncates and rewrites dist/. The release suite runs up to 4 test files concurrently, so one file's tsc rewrote dist/ while another file's npm pack archived it, and node-tar failed with EOF 'encountered unexpected EOF' on a dist file. --silent suppressed that npm error, so the test diagnostic showed only the prepare script's benign 'npm pack: skipping merge-driver install during artifact creation' line. Seen on main 131dc3a (test (22): bisect.test.ts walk-killed test) and on #177 (test (26): checkpoints.test.ts installed-CLI test). Reproduced locally: 3/60 and 5/60 staggered concurrent packs failed with EOF on dist files."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[4]: ci,concurrency,flaky-test,testing
created_at: "2026-11-04T09:32:51.686Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-04T09:33:02.246Z"
assignee: claude-hub
claim_principal: claude-hub
author: claude-hub
estimated_minutes: 60
acceptance_criteria: installPackedExtension packs the existing build with --ignore-scripts (as composition-consumer.test.ts and verify-pack-privacy.ts already do) and --loglevel=error so npm's own error reaches the diagnostic; a regression test proves a real pack leaves every dist/ file mtime unchanged and fails when the old --silent arguments are restored; 60 staggered concurrent packs with the new arguments all succeed with empty stderr.
severity: high
expected_result: Concurrent test files pack the extension without corrupting each other's archive.
component: scripts/pm-environment
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-04T09:33:02.246Z",claude-hub,"Verified 2026-11-04: the new test passes with the fix and fails with the old --silent arguments restored (dist mtimes changed). Stress test of 60 staggered concurrent packs: old args 3/60 and 5/60 failed (npm error code EOF, syscall read, path dist/engine/lifecycle.js, dist/ledger.js, dist/engine/destruction.js.map); new args 0/60 failed, all stderr empty. typecheck, lint, docstring, duplicates pass; test/quality-scripts.test.ts 10/10. Every runner builds before packing: test, coverage, release:check, and the Windows job's npm run build step."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/pm-environment.ts,project,pack arguments reuse the build and keep npm errors
  test/quality-scripts.test.ts,project,shared-build regression and argv expectation
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref},note}:
  npm run build && node --test --test-name-pattern=pack test/quality-scripts.test.ts,project,300,claude-hub,"2026-11-04T09:33:01.450Z",local_mutation,fix/serialize-packed-extension-installs,"pack argv, failure paths and shared-build regression"
